attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a two-column spine.** Columns 0 to 1, `gcvH` to `gcvP`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99.6 to 100% of them, fewest at column 1, `gcvP`, 99.6% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column follows**, column 2, `ygfF`, carried by 53%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2.c2, P}. Then columns 3 to 15, `bglA` to `idi`, are a spine carried by 93 to 95%, [[tRNA modification and glycine cleavage]] {S3, Q}. Through columns 45 to 48 a branch of 4 shell families runs in 18 to 21%, [[type III secretion]] {S12.b45, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.34 against 0.47 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 41, `yqeF`, a fork column, 2.00 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 44 to 79, `araE` to `ygdI`, are carried by 11 to 89%, in a region of plasticity in 16 to 67% of calls {S12}. The last column is `ygdI`, in 23% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.43 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.69 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 88% against 95% {C}.

